<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n72779" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄκρῐς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιος</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>jagged point</i> or <i>prominence, any roughness</i> on
			an edge or surface, as of a fractured bone, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Art.</u>
				14
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as Adj.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀκρίς, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>,
					ὁ, ἡ,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀκριόεις</span>
			, <i>rugged,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φάραγξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					1016
				</span></i>
			. (Cf. Umbr. <i>ocar</i> (acc. <i>ocrem,</i> etc.) 'arx,
			mons', OLat. <i>ocris = mons confragosus.</i>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
